Falsifies `elf::verification::page_range_is_panic_free_and_ordered`.

The defect: the round back up to a page boundary multiplies without saturating. After a
`div_ceil` the multiply looks like it is putting back exactly what was taken out, which is what
makes the saturation read as belt and braces, and the comment two lines above only defends the
`saturating_add`.

Expected to fail: the panic-free half of the claim, as an arithmetic overflow, at a `vaddr` near
`u64::MAX`, where the saturated sum divides to a quotient whose product with the page size does
not fit. `Segment` is `pub`, so it must hold without `parse`'s guarantees.

